course: dictionary
lesson: 10800
title: A very rare animal
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A vaquita is a very small porpoise, a sea animal that breathes air and is related to dolphins. It lives only in the northern Gulf of California, in Mexico, so you will not find it anywhere else. «The vaquita, a porpoise in Mexico, is the rarest sea mammal.» Rarest means there are fewer of them than any other sea mammal.
explain: Rare and endangered go together here. Endangered means in danger of dying out. Scientists say the vaquita is the most endangered sea mammal in the world, and only around ten were counted in recent surveys. A survey is a careful count done to find out how many animals are left.
explain: Why are there so few? Vaquitas get caught in fishing nets. When a whole animal is lost this way, the number of vaquitas keeps falling. Read the clues in the sentence to work out what the words mean, just as you would with any new word.
fact: A vaquita is a very small porpoise.
fact: It lives only in the northern Gulf of California, in Mexico.
fact: «Vaquita» is Spanish for «little cow».
fact: It has dark rings around its eyes, like a panda.
fact: Vaquitas are close to extinction, which means they are in danger of disappearing for ever.
exercise: «The vaquita, a porpoise in Mexico, is the rarest sea mammal.» What is a vaquita? | A large whale | *A very small porpoise | A bird that lives on cliffs | A kind of fish with a shell
exercise: Where does the vaquita live? | In the rivers of Spain | In every ocean in the world | On dry land, far from the sea | *Only in the northern Gulf of California, in Mexico
exercise: Its name is Spanish. What does «vaquita» mean? | Sea giant | Dark eyes | Little fish | *Little cow
test: Why are there only about ten vaquitas left? | They move to a new ocean every year | They only eat very large fish | *They get caught in fishing nets | They are too fast to be counted
test: What does «endangered» mean? | Very large in size | Full of bright colours | Easy to find in the sea | *In danger of dying out
exam: The vaquita is close to extinction. What does this most nearly mean? | Growing very quickly | Found in every sea in the world | *Almost gone for ever | Sleeping very deeply
